virglrenderer: scanout buffers as IOSurfaces (prototype, off by default)

What: with OMACVM_SCANOUT_IOSURFACE=1, a single-level 8-bit BGRX/BGRA 2D
buffer the guest makes for scanout (VIRGL_RES_BIND_SCANOUT) lives in an
IOSurface bound as a RECTANGLE texture, so QEMU can put the buffer itself on
the window (omacvm-cocoa-present-direct.patch) instead of drawing it into a
present surface. Writes and framebuffer reads go to the IOSurface as before;
samplers cannot read a RECTANGLE texture as 2D, so they read a 2D shadow,
copied once per submit when a draw samples the buffer.
The guest's page flip completes in the guest without waiting for the Mac, so
the guest may draw into a buffer that is still on the window, queued in
QEMU's present, or still held by WindowServer (it keeps the frame shown
before the current one in use). A write into a buffer still in use
(IOSurfaceIsInUse) moves the buffer to a free IOSurface (a spare, at most two
per buffer) with its picture copied on the GPU, as Hyprland redraws only
what changed. Only when no IOSurface is free does the write wait, at most
25 ms. A plain wait stalled Hyprland's three-buffer swapchain at 60 frames a
second (every third write waited the full 25 ms: WindowServer kept the
buffer until a newer frame came, and the wait kept that frame from coming).
stderr every 5 s: writes, waits, moves, shadow copies.
Why: QEMU's present draw costs 0.45 ms of GPU per frame at 5K
(docs/experiments/display-path.md, "Scanout zero copy: prototype").
Limits (review of the prototype): 8-bit SDR only (a 10-bit scanout stays a
plain texture); up to two spare IOSurfaces per buffer (59 MB each at 5K) and
the shadow, none of them charged to the guest's memory budget; only a new
framebuffer state and a blit into the buffer are checked (a draw through a
framebuffer left bound, a clear, a copy or an upload write as they are), and
a timed-out wait writes anyway; a move re-points the texture in place, so
another context's framebuffer keeps the old IOSurface until it is set again;
the shadow is refreshed once per submit and takes the last view's swizzle;
the shader blitter still samples such a buffer as 2D; internal copies run
under the guest's conditional rendering.
TODO(revert: prototype on branch present-direct-surface, not for main as it is).
Upstream: not sent (macOS only).
Tests: none at build time; VM A/B in docs/experiments/display-path.md.
